[2026-11-18] fix: the eight defects from the independent QA review of the boss and loot work
  files: game/arena.py, game/props.py, game/bosses.py, game/player.py, game/gfx.py, game/ally.py, tests/test_boss_mechanics.py, tests/test_maker.py
  why:   QA review (verdict ship with notes). D1 a dead boss's tractor beam stayed on screen (beam drawn only while the boss is alive; beam reset on defeat). D2 the tractor beam could lift a hero off the top of the screen (a ceiling at FLOOR-150). D3 the tutorial pointed at a Gear key that did nothing (the gear screen now works in the tutorial). D5 lifesteal rounded every hit up to 1 HP (fractions now carry over). D6 gravestone zombies were uncapped (same cap of 4 as the boss's summons). D7 the wave clock ran while the Gear screen was open, so a wave could spawn all at once (the clock now only runs in battle). D8 a grab rooted a hero even when it was dodged or blocked, and a downed hero kept the root (root only on a landed hit; cleared when downed). D9 the wave number overprinted the level title (it is now part of the title). D10 chest card text ran past the card (text is measured with the UI font). D12 a crystal or orb could be broken while its boss was still entering (immune until the entrance ends). D13 bosses spawned from dev Y had no setup (every boss spawn now runs setup). D14 the CPU chest pick took a worse item for a slot (it now needs a real upgrade). D4 (the ally looting the human's corpses) is handled by the ally change below.
  notes: test_boss_mechanics grab test now gives the hero a hittable state (the grab is correctly a no-op on an invulnerable hero). Not fixed (nits, listed in README Known issues): class-select title overlap, hard-to-read boss text, RESISTED overlap, thorns vs bullets.

[2026-11-18] feat: the CPU ally is an assistant, not a second player
  files: game/ally.py, game/player.py, game/arena.py, tests/test_maker.py, README.md
  why:   the owner sat and watched the CPU do everything. The ally now: never loots corpses (they are the human's); takes a boss-chest item only after the human has chosen; stays within 80 px of the human and returns when more than 150 px away; fights only foes within 130 px of the human; reacts to a boss wind-up only after 0.35 s; casts skill 1 every 9 s and skill 2 every 14 s. Its hits are 40% weaker and its cooldowns 50% longer (Player.recompute, cpu flag). The CPU's handicap now applies even with no gear (Arena recomputes every hero).
