[2026-11-18] feat: ELEGOO MEGA 2560 hand controller drives player 1 (serial bridge, reader thread, gesture logic)
  files: game/padbridge.py (new), game/inputs.py, game/app.py, main.py, tests/test_padbridge.py (new), docs/controller-protocol.md (rewritten), README.md, pyproject.toml, uv.lock
  why:   owner's custom pad (MEGA 2560 + GY-521 + 2 buttons + joystick + stick click) sends 8 CSV fields at about 20 Hz over /dev/cu.usbmodem1301. Built as a Motion subclass (PadMotion) instead of injecting OS key presses with pynput: no macOS accessibility permission, no typing into other windows, and gameplay code is unchanged. The keyboard still works alongside it, and the pad also drives the menus (stick moves, button 1 confirms).
  notes: pyserial 3.5 added (uv add pyserial). Verified against the real board for six seconds: every line parses (0 bad), calibration completes, the resting baseline is set. NOT verified with a human hand: gesture thresholds (SWING_DELTA, SHOVE_DELTA, SHIELD_TILT) are first guesses; tune with main.py --pad-monitor. The board has no gyro, so gestures are accelerometer-based. Esc still goes back on the keyboard only (the pad has no back button).

