[2026-11-20] fix: correction to the 2026-11-19 nunchuck firmware entry (it sits inside an older entry above, not at the bottom)
  files: changes.log, arduino_nunchuck/arduino_nunchuck.ino
  why:   that entry says the nunchuck connects to 5V; the original Wii nunchuck is a 3.3V part. Its real contact order (connector seen from the front) is top row SCL, GND and bottom row 3.3V, SDA. It was never made to read on the owner's unit: the bus timed out with it connected while another I2C device (0x68) scanned fine, so the nunchuck or its adapter is suspect. The entry was not edited (the log is append only).

