  files: game/gfx.py, game/padbridge.py, game/app.py, README.md
  why:   owner asked for PS2 menu and control hints that show the real button shape instead of letters (square, not "SQ"). gfx.text() now draws tokens like {cross} as glyphs (glyph()), PS2_NAMES maps buttons and D-pad directions to those tokens, and app.hint() shows a glyph footer in menus when the PS2 pad is the active controller.
